The BLAK paper (yIdCQFvbYe), most similar in topic (Koopman + time-varying + control), averaged ~5.8 and was rejected — it also had missing adaptive Koopman baselines and real-world experiments. MamKO is somewhat weaker than BLAK: BLAK compared against multiple Koopman-UQ methods and included real truck data; MamKO avoids all time-varying Koopman competitors entirely and stays simulation-only. The Mamba mischaracterization is an additional systematic framing error absent from BLAK.

